@brandonburrus Heads up — the first repro in this issue is fixed in our fork, [zombie-mermaid](https://github.com/dfadler/zombie-mermaid), a maintained fork of beautiful-mermaid: `A ~~~ B` invisible-link syntax is now parsed and participates in layout ordering (drawn with no line/connector/arrowhead).

Fixed by [PR #206](https://github.com/dfadler/zombie-mermaid/pull/206), commit [`673d3da`](https://github.com/dfadler/zombie-mermaid/commit/673d3da22305af381ac167e85d4b17fb20427dc6), shipped in [v1.3.0](https://github.com/dfadler/zombie-mermaid/releases/tag/v1.3.0).

I haven't confirmed a fix for the second repro (per-subgraph `direction` leaking diagram-wide) — flagging that as still open on our end too, so leaving this issue as-is rather than claiming full resolution.
